            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Domitian</strong><br>\nDomitian was born on October 24, 51 AD, to Vespasian, a successful military general, and Flavia Domitilla. He grew up during a period of great turmoil for Rome, known as the Year of the Four Emperors. After the death of Nero, Rome was without a stable leader until Vespasian became emperor in 69 AD. Domitian had an older brother, Titus, who would also become emperor before him. Despite his noble birth, Domitian’s early life was overshadowed by his brother’s achievements and his father’s military campaigns.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nUpon the death of his father in 79 AD, Domitian's brother, Titus, assumed the role of emperor. Domitian held the title of Caesar and took on a variety of administrative duties, but he had limited actual power. When Titus died unexpectedly in 81 AD, Domitian became the emperor of Rome. His ascension marked the continuation of the Flavian dynasty established by his father, and he started his rule with the promise of restoring the strength and prosperity of Rome.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Domitian's Reign</strong><br>\nAs emperor, Domitian strengthened the economy by revaluing the Roman currency and expanded the military defenses of the empire. He was known for his autocratic rule and efforts to increase the role and visibility of the emperor. Domitian also initiated a major building program, restoring and constructing temples, stadiums, and other public buildings to revitalize Rome after the damage of past civil wars.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
